IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cbca-core-definitions`
IMPORT `cb4-common`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part XVIII, ss 214 to 220: LIQUIDATION AND
-- DISSOLUTION BY A COURT.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Department of Justice Canada consolidation
-- current to 2026-09-30; not verified against the official text.
--
-- WHAT THIS MODULE IS. The extra grounds on which a shareholder may ask a court to liquidate and dissolve a
-- corporation (s 214), the paper the court needs (s 216), the long list of orders it may make (s 217), and
-- what happens when a liquidation order is made: it commences, the corporation stops trading, the directors'
-- and shareholders' powers pass to the liquidator, and the court may appoint the liquidator (ss 218 to 220).
-- Sections 241 (oppression) and 242 (procedure) are other pieces' (cb5); s 155 is cb3's; s 223 is in
-- cb4-liquidator.
--
-- A court's "may" is encoded as a BOOLEAN that is TRUE when the Act lets the court act. Whether the court
-- WILL act is for the court.
--
-- "Four weeks after the date of the order" (s 216(2)) is 28 days, the order's date being day 0 (keel fork F1).

§§ `s 214 Further grounds`

-- (1)(a): three alternative routes to the same finding: the court is satisfied that an act or omission,
-- the manner in which the business is carried on, or the manner in which the directors' powers are
-- exercised, is oppressive or unfairly prejudicial to, or unfairly disregards, the interests of any security
-- holder, creditor, director or officer.
-- src:2694 | Further grounds
-- src:2695 | 214 (1) A court may order the liquidation and dissolution of a corporation or any of its affiliated corporations on the application of a shareholder,
-- src:2696 | (a) if the court is satisfied that in respect of a corporation or any of its affiliates
-- src:2697 | (i) any act or omission of the corporation or any of its affiliates effects a result,
-- src:2698 | (ii) the business or affairs of the corporation or any of its affiliates are or have been carried on or conducted in a manner, or
-- src:2699 | (iii) the powers of the directors of the corporation or any of its affiliates are or have been exercised in a manner
-- src:2700 | that is oppressive or unfairly prejudicial to or that unfairly disregards the interests of any security holder, creditor, director or officer; or
@ref CBCA s 214(1)(a) (src:2696-2700)
GIVEN `an act or omission of the corporation or an affiliate effects a result that is oppressive or unfairly prejudicial to or unfairly disregards the interests of a security holder, creditor, director or officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the business or affairs of the corporation or an affiliate are or have been carried on in a manner that is oppressive or unfairly prejudicial to or unfairly disregards the interests of a security holder, creditor, director or officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the powers of the directors of the corporation or an affiliate are or have been exercised in a manner that is oppressive or unfairly prejudicial to or unfairly disregards the interests of a security holder, creditor, director or officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court is satisfied of oppression within s 214(1)(a)` MEANS
        `an act or omission of the corporation or an affiliate effects a result that is oppressive or unfairly prejudicial to or unfairly disregards the interests of a security holder, creditor, director or officer`
    OR  `the business or affairs of the corporation or an affiliate are or have been carried on in a manner that is oppressive or unfairly prejudicial to or unfairly disregards the interests of a security holder, creditor, director or officer`
    OR  `the powers of the directors of the corporation or an affiliate are or have been exercised in a manner that is oppressive or unfairly prejudicial to or unfairly disregards the interests of a security holder, creditor, director or officer`

-- src:2701 | (b) if the court is satisfied that
-- src:2702 | (i) a unanimous shareholder agreement entitles a complaining shareholder to demand dissolution of the corporation after the occurrence of a specified event and that event has occurred, or
-- src:2703 | (ii) it is just and equitable that the corporation should be liquidated and dissolved.
@ref CBCA s 214(1)(b) (src:2701-2703)
GIVEN `a unanimous shareholder agreement entitles a complaining shareholder to demand dissolution after the occurrence of a specified event` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that event has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is just and equitable that the corporation should be liquidated and dissolved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court is satisfied of a ground within s 214(1)(b)` MEANS
        (    `a unanimous shareholder agreement entitles a complaining shareholder to demand dissolution after the occurrence of a specified event`
         AND `that event has occurred`)
    OR  `it is just and equitable that the corporation should be liquidated and dissolved`

@ref CBCA s 214(1) (src:2695)
GIVEN `the applicant is a shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `oppression is made out under paragraph 214(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a ground is made out under paragraph 214(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a court may order the liquidation and dissolution of the corporation or an affiliate within s 214(1)` MEANS
        `the applicant is a shareholder`
    AND (    `oppression is made out under paragraph 214(1)(a)`
         OR  `a ground is made out under paragraph 214(1)(b)`)

-- src:2704 | Alternative order
-- src:2705 | (2) On an application under this section, a court may make such order under this section or section 241 as it thinks fit.
@ref CBCA s 214(2) (src:2705)
GIVEN `an application has been made under section 214` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court may make an order under section 214 or section 241 within s 214(2)` MEANS
    `an application has been made under section 214`

-- src:2706 | Application of s. 242
-- src:2707 | (3) Section 242 applies to an application under this section.
@ref CBCA s 214(3) (src:2707)
GIVEN `an application has been made under section 214` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 242 applies to the application within s 214(3)` MEANS
    `an application has been made under section 214`

§§ `s 215 Application for supervision; court supervision`

-- src:2708 | Application for supervision
-- src:2709 | 215 (1) An application to a court to supervise a voluntary liquidation and dissolution under subsection 211(8) shall state the reasons, verified by an affidavit of the applicant, why the court should supervise the liquidation and dissolution.
@ref CBCA s 215(1) (src:2709)
GIVEN `the application states the reasons why the court should supervise the liquidation and dissolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reasons are verified by an affidavit of the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the application for supervision complies with s 215(1)` MEANS
        `the application states the reasons why the court should supervise the liquidation and dissolution`
    AND `the reasons are verified by an affidavit of the applicant`

-- src:2710 | Court supervision
-- src:2711 | (2) If a court makes an order applied for under subsection 211(8), the liquidation and dissolution of the corporation shall continue under the supervision of the court in accordance with this Act.
@ref CBCA s 215(2) (src:2711)
GIVEN `a court has made an order applied for under subsection 211(8)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the liquidation and dissolution continues under the supervision of the court within s 215(2)` MEANS
    `a court has made an order applied for under subsection 211(8)`

§§ `s 216 Application to court; show cause; information; publication`

-- src:2712 | Application to court
-- src:2713 | 216 (1) An application to a court under subsection 214(1) shall state the reasons, verified by an affidavit of the applicant, why the corporation should be liquidated and dissolved.
@ref CBCA s 216(1) (src:2713)
GIVEN `the application states the reasons why the corporation should be liquidated and dissolved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reasons are verified by an affidavit of the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the application under s 214(1) complies with s 216(1)` MEANS
        `the application states the reasons why the corporation should be liquidated and dissolved`
    AND `the reasons are verified by an affidavit of the applicant`

-- src:2714 | Show cause order
-- src:2715 | (2) On an application under subsection 214(1), the court may make an order requiring the corporation and any person having an interest in the corporation or claim against it to show cause, at a time and place specified in the order, within four weeks after the date of the order, why the corporation should not be liquidated and dissolved.
@ref CBCA s 216(2) (src:2715)
GIVEN `an application has been made under subsection 214(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court may order the corporation and persons interested to show cause within s 216(2)` MEANS
    `an application has been made under subsection 214(1)`

@ref CBCA s 216(2) (src:2715)
GIVEN `the date of the order` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the show cause time within s 216(2)` MEANS
    `the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 4, `unit of time` IS `calendar weeks`) `counted from` `the date of the order`

@ref CBCA s 216(2) (src:2715)
GIVEN `the date of the order` IS A DATE
      `the time specified in the order for showing cause` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the time specified for showing cause is within four weeks after the order within s 216(2)` MEANS
    `done within the time limit` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 4, `unit of time` IS `calendar weeks`) `the date of the order` `the time specified in the order for showing cause`

-- src:2716 | Powers of court
-- src:2717 | (3) On an application under subsection 214(1), the court may order the directors and officers of the corporation to furnish the court with all material information known to or reasonably ascertainable by them, including
-- src:2718 | (a) financial statements of the corporation;
-- src:2719 | (b) the name and address of each shareholder of the corporation; and
-- src:2720 | (c) the name and address of each known creditor or claimant, including any creditor or claimant with unliquidated, future or contingent claims, and any person with whom the corporation has a contract.
@ref CBCA s 216(3) (src:2717-2720)
GIVEN `an application has been made under subsection 214(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court may order the directors and officers to furnish all material information within s 216(3)` MEANS
    `an application has been made under subsection 214(1)`

-- The three named items are examples ("including"): each is within the order if known or reasonably
-- ascertainable, whether or not it would otherwise be called material.
@ref CBCA s 216(3) (src:2717-2720)
GIVEN `the information is of a kind named in paragraph 216(3)(a), (b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is material` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is known to or reasonably ascertainable by the directors and officers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the information is within the order the court may make within s 216(3)` MEANS
        `it is known to or reasonably ascertainable by the directors and officers`
    AND (    `the information is of a kind named in paragraph 216(3)(a), (b) or (c)`
         OR  `the information is material`)

-- src:2721 | Publication
-- src:2722 | (4) A copy of an order made under subsection (2) shall be
-- src:2723 | (a) published as directed in the order, at least once in each week before the time appointed for the hearing, in a newspaper published or distributed in the place where the corporation has its registered office; and
-- src:2724 | (b) served on the Director and each person named in the order.
@ref CBCA s 216(4) (src:2722-2724)
GIVEN `a copy of the order was published as directed in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was published at least once in each week before the time appointed for the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was published in a newspaper published or distributed in the place where the corporation has its registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy was served on the Director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy was served on each person named in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the order under s 216(2) has been published and served as s 216(4) requires` MEANS
        `a copy of the order was published as directed in the order`
    AND `it was published at least once in each week before the time appointed for the hearing`
    AND `it was published in a newspaper published or distributed in the place where the corporation has its registered office`
    AND `a copy was served on the Director`
    AND `a copy was served on each person named in the order`

-- src:2725 | Person responsible
-- src:2726 | (5) Publication and service of an order under this section shall be effected by the corporation or by such other person and in such manner as the court may order.
@ref CBCA s 216(5) (src:2726)
GIVEN `the person is the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has ordered that other person to publish and serve` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the publication and service are in the manner the court has ordered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`publication and service are effected by the right person in the right manner within s 216(5)` MEANS
        (    `the person is the corporation`
         OR  `the court has ordered that other person to publish and serve`)
    AND `the publication and service are in the manner the court has ordered`

§§ `s 217 Powers of court`

-- The gate is the court's satisfaction that the corporation can pay or provide for ALL its obligations;
-- the paragraphs say what the court may then order. Paragraphs (j), (k), (l), (n) and (o) carry conditions.
-- src:2727 | Powers of court
-- src:2728 | 217 In connection with the dissolution or the liquidation and dissolution of a corporation, the court may, if it is satisfied that the corporation is able to pay or adequately provide for the discharge of all its obligations, make any order it thinks fit including, without limiting the generality of the foregoing,
-- src:2729 | (a) an order to liquidate;
-- src:2730 | (b) an order appointing a liquidator, with or without security, fixing the liquidator’s remuneration and replacing a liquidator;
-- src:2731 | (c) an order appointing inspectors or referees, specifying their powers, fixing their remuneration and replacing inspectors or referees;
-- src:2732 | (d) an order determining the notice to be given to any interested person, or dispensing with notice to any person;
-- src:2733 | (e) an order determining the validity of any claims made against the corporation;
-- src:2734 | (f) an order, at any stage of the proceedings, restraining the directors and officers from
-- src:2735 | (i) exercising any of their powers, or
-- src:2736 | (ii) collecting or receiving any debt or other property of the corporation, and from paying out or transferring any property of the corporation, except as permitted by the court;
-- src:2737 | (g) an order determining and enforcing the duty or liability of any present or former director, officer or shareholder
-- src:2738 | (i) to the corporation, or
-- src:2739 | (ii) for an obligation of the corporation;
-- src:2740 | (h) an order approving the payment, satisfaction or compromise of claims against the corporation and the retention of assets for such purpose, and determining the adequacy of provisions for the payment or discharge of obligations of the corporation, whether liquidated, unliquidated, future or contingent;
-- src:2741 | (i) an order disposing of or destroying the documents and records of the corporation;
-- src:2742 | (j) on the application of a creditor, the inspectors or the liquidator, an order giving directions on any matter arising in the liquidation;
-- src:2743 | (k) after notice has been given to all interested parties, an order relieving a liquidator from any omission or default on such terms as the court thinks fit and confirming any act of the liquidator;
-- src:2744 | (l) subject to section 223, an order approving any proposed interim or final distribution to shareholders in money or in property;
-- src:2745 | (m) an order disposing of any property belonging to creditors or shareholders who cannot be found;
-- src:2746 | (n) on the application of any director, officer, security holder, creditor or the liquidator,
-- src:2747 | (i) an order staying the liquidation on such terms and conditions as the court thinks fit,
-- src:2748 | (ii) an order continuing or discontinuing the liquidation proceedings, or
-- src:2749 | (iii) an order to the liquidator to restore to the corporation all its remaining property; and
-- src:2750 | (o) after the liquidator has rendered a final account to the court, an order dissolving the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 217 (src:2728-2750)
DECLARE `Kind of order under s 217` IS ONE OF
    `an order to liquidate (s 217(a))`
    `an order appointing a liquidator, with or without security, fixing the liquidator's remuneration or replacing a liquidator (s 217(b))`
    `an order appointing inspectors or referees, specifying their powers, fixing their remuneration or replacing them (s 217(c))`
    `an order determining the notice to be given to any interested person, or dispensing with notice to any person (s 217(d))`
    `an order determining the validity of any claims made against the corporation (s 217(e))`
    `an order, at any stage, restraining the directors and officers from exercising any of their powers, or from collecting or receiving any debt or other property of the corporation or paying out or transferring any property, except as the court permits (s 217(f))`
    `an order determining and enforcing the duty or liability of a present or former director, officer or shareholder to the corporation or for an obligation of the corporation (s 217(g))`
    `an order approving the payment, satisfaction or compromise of claims and the retention of assets for that purpose, and determining the adequacy of provisions for obligations (s 217(h))`
    `an order disposing of or destroying the documents and records of the corporation (s 217(i))`
    `an order giving directions on a matter arising in the liquidation (s 217(j))`
    `an order relieving a liquidator from an omission or default and confirming an act of the liquidator (s 217(k))`
    `an order approving a proposed interim or final distribution to shareholders in money or in property (s 217(l))`
    `an order disposing of any property belonging to creditors or shareholders who cannot be found (s 217(m))`
    `an order staying the liquidation, continuing or discontinuing the liquidation proceedings, or directing the liquidator to restore the remaining property to the corporation (s 217(n))`
    `an order dissolving the corporation after the liquidator's final account (s 217(o))`
    `any other order the court thinks fit under s 217`

@ref CBCA s 217 (src:2728)
GIVEN `the order is made in connection with the dissolution or the liquidation and dissolution of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the corporation is able to pay or adequately provide for the discharge of all its obligations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court may make an order under the opening words of s 217` MEANS
        `the order is made in connection with the dissolution or the liquidation and dissolution of the corporation`
    AND `the court is satisfied that the corporation is able to pay or adequately provide for the discharge of all its obligations`

@ref CBCA s 217(j), (k), (l), (n), (o) (src:2742-2750)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of order under s 217`
      `the court may make an order under the opening words of s 217` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is a creditor, the inspectors or the liquidator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice has been given to all interested parties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 223 permits the distribution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is a director, officer, security holder, creditor or the liquidator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the liquidator has rendered a final account to the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court may make this kind of order within s 217` MEANS
        `the court may make an order under the opening words of s 217`
    AND (CONSIDER kind
         WHEN `an order giving directions on a matter arising in the liquidation (s 217(j))` THEN `the applicant is a creditor, the inspectors or the liquidator`
         WHEN `an order relieving a liquidator from an omission or default and confirming an act of the liquidator (s 217(k))` THEN `notice has been given to all interested parties`
         WHEN `an order approving a proposed interim or final distribution to shareholders in money or in property (s 217(l))` THEN `section 223 permits the distribution`
         WHEN `an order staying the liquidation, continuing or discontinuing the liquidation proceedings, or directing the liquidator to restore the remaining property to the corporation (s 217(n))` THEN `the applicant is a director, officer, security holder, creditor or the liquidator`
         WHEN `an order dissolving the corporation after the liquidator's final account (s 217(o))` THEN `the liquidator has rendered a final account to the court`
         OTHERWISE TRUE)

§§ `ss 218 to 220 Effect of an order; liquidator`

-- src:2751 | Effect of order
-- src:2752 | 218 The liquidation of a corporation commences when a court makes an order therefor.
@ref CBCA s 218 (src:2752)
GIVEN `the date the court makes the order for liquidation` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the liquidation has commenced on a day within s 218` MEANS
    `the day asked about` AT LEAST `the date the court makes the order for liquidation`

-- (1)(a): the corporation continues in existence but stops carrying on business, except the business that
-- is, in the liquidator's opinion, required for an orderly liquidation.
-- src:2753 | Cessation of business and powers
-- src:2754 | 219 (1) If a court makes an order for liquidation of a corporation,
-- src:2755 | (a) the corporation continues in existence but shall cease to carry on business, except the business that is, in the opinion of the liquidator, required for an orderly liquidation; and
@ref CBCA s 219(1)(a) (src:2754-2755)
GIVEN `a court has made an order for liquidation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the business is, in the opinion of the liquidator, required for an orderly liquidation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may carry on the business within s 219(1)(a)` MEANS
        (NOT `a court has made an order for liquidation`)
    OR  `the business is, in the opinion of the liquidator, required for an orderly liquidation`

@ref CBCA s 219(1)(a) (src:2754-2755)
GIVEN `a court has made an order for liquidation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation continues in existence within s 219(1)(a)` MEANS
    `a court has made an order for liquidation`

-- src:2756 | (b) the powers of the directors and shareholders cease and vest in the liquidator, except as specifically authorized by the court.
@ref CBCA s 219(1)(b) (src:2756)
GIVEN `a court has made an order for liquidation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has specifically authorized the directors or shareholders to keep the power` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the powers of the directors and shareholders cease and vest in the liquidator within s 219(1)(b)` MEANS
        `a court has made an order for liquidation`
    AND (NOT `the court has specifically authorized the directors or shareholders to keep the power`)

-- src:2757 | Delegation by liquidator
-- src:2758 | (2) The liquidator may delegate any powers vested in the liquidator by paragraph (1)(b) to the directors or shareholders.
@ref CBCA s 219(2) (src:2758)
GIVEN `the power is vested in the liquidator by paragraph 219(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the delegate is the directors or the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the liquidator may delegate the power within s 219(2)` MEANS
        `the power is vested in the liquidator by paragraph 219(1)(b)`
    AND `the delegate is the directors or the shareholders`

@ref CBCA s 220(1) (src:2760)
GIVEN `the court is making an order for the liquidation of the corporation, or has made one` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court may appoint a person as liquidator within s 220(1)` MEANS
    `the court is making an order for the liquidation of the corporation, or has made one`

-- src:2759 | Appointment of liquidator
-- src:2760 | 220 (1) When making an order for the liquidation of a corporation or at any time thereafter, the court may appoint any person, including a director, an officer or a shareholder of the corporation or any other body corporate, as liquidator of the corporation.
-- src:2761 | Vacancy
-- src:2762 | (2) Where an order for the liquidation of a corporation has been made and the office of liquidator is or becomes vacant, the property of the corporation is under the control of the court until the office of liquidator is filled.
@ref CBCA s 220(2) (src:2762)
GIVEN `an order for the liquidation of the corporation has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the office of liquidator is vacant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the property of the corporation is under the control of the court within s 220(2)` MEANS
        `an order for the liquidation of the corporation has been made`
    AND `the office of liquidator is vacant`
